{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","max_tokens":768,"stream":true,"system":"Keep the answer short.","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Find the unique integer selector from 1 through 99 that has remainder 2 when divided by 5, remainder 0 when divided by 7, and remainder 7 when divided by 11. Work out the constraints before answering. State the selector with a short explanation."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Solve x ≡ 2 (mod 5), x ≡ 0 (mod 7), x ≡ 7 (mod 11).\n\nMultiples of 7 that are ≡ 7 (mod 11): x = 7k, so 7k ≡ 7 (mod 11), giving k ≡ 1 (mod 11). So x = 7, 84, 161, ... (x ≡ 7 mod 77).\n\nNow x ≡ 2 (mod 5):\n- 7 mod 5 = 2 ✓.\n\nSo x = 7 works. Check: 7 mod 5 = 2, 7 mod 7 = 0, 7 mod 11 = 7. ✓\n\nThe moduli combine to 385, so the solution is unique in 1 through 385, and in particular in 1 through 99.\n\n**Selector: 7**\n\nThe conditions mod 7 and mod 11 force x ≡ 7 (mod 77), leaving candidates 7 and 84 in range. Of these, only 7 leaves remainder 2 when divided by 5 (84 leaves 4)."}]},{"role":"user","content":"Now reply exactly OK."}],"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}}